{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.TypedGarsideElement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.TypedGarsideElement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideElement","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L102-L107","doc":"Top-level Prop alias matching the manifest `lean.ref`\n`qou:QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideElement`. The named claim is the\npure-proton collapse: the `pp` typed crossing coefficient vanishes. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:typed-garside-element","label":"def:typed-garside-element","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pure_proton_garside_is_standard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pure_proton_garside_is_standard","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L87-L100","doc":"**Pure-proton crossing coefficients vanish.** For the pure proton\nordering `[p, p, …, p]` every pairwise crossing is `pp`-type, and the\ntyped crossing coefficient `d(p, p) = 0`. Hence every typed crossing\n`C(p, p; σ) = σ + d(p, p) = σ` is the *untyped* generator, so the\ntyped Garside element equals the standard Garside element `Δ_A`.\n\nThe Lean content is the vanishing of the `pp` coefficient, which is\nexactly the algebraic reason the typing collapses to the standard\nelement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.typed_garside_leading_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.typed_garside_leading_term","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L78-L85","doc":"**Leading-term theorem (conditional on `TypedGarsideLeadingTerm`).**\nThe leading term of the typed Garside element of any nuclear ordering\n`ord` (arity ≥ 2) is the standard Garside word `Δ_{|ord|}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm.leading_eq_garside","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm.leading_eq_garside","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The conjectural content: for every nuclear ordering of arity ≥ 2,\nthe typed Garside element's leading term is the standard Garside\nelement on `|ord|` strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm.garsideWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm.garsideWord","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The standard Garside word `Δ_A = σ₀(σ₁σ₀)⋯` on `|ord|` strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm.leadingWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm.leadingWord","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The leading (degree-lex maximal) word of the typed Garside element\nof a nuclear ordering, as a braid word (list of generator\nindices). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TypedGarsideLeadingTerm","kind":"class","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L56-L76","doc":"**Leading-term structural input.** The typed Garside element has the\nstandard Garside element `Δ_A` as its leading term (highest\ndegree-lex word), independent of the typing: the `d`-shifts only\naffect lower-order terms. The full proof requires the\nGröbner–Shirshov normal-form infrastructure for `H_A(q)`; we\naxiomatise the leading-term identity as a class field encoding the\ngenuine content — the leading word equals the standard Garside word\n`Δ_A` for every admissible nuclear ordering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.garside_crossing_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.garside_crossing_count","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L44-L54","doc":"The total number of pairwise crossings in the Garside staircase\nfor A nucleons is C(A, 2) = A(A-1)/2.\n\nThe hypothesis `_hA : 2 ≤ A` is preserved (with leading-\nunderscore) for documentation consistency with the minimum-\narity assumption in `def:typed-garside-element`, even though\n`Nat.choose_two_right` holds for all `A : ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.neutronCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.neutronCount","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L40-L42","doc":"Number of neutrons in an ordering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.protonCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.protonCount","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L36-L38","doc":"Number of protons in an ordering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearOrdering","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearOrdering","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L33-L34","doc":"A nuclear ordering is a list of nucleon types. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.typedCrossingCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.typedCrossingCoeff","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L24-L31","doc":"Typed crossing coefficient d(f_i, f_j) for the Hecke algebra.\npp → 0, nn → -h, pn/np → -h/2 where h = q - q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instReprNucleonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instReprNucleonType","kind":"instance","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instReprNucleonType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instReprNucleonType.repr","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqNucleonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqNucleonType","kind":"instance","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType.neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType.neutron","kind":"ctor","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L21-L21","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType.proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType.proton","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType","kind":"inductive","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/typed-garside-element.lean#L18-L22","doc":"Nucleon type: proton or neutron. ","signatureChunk":0}]}